{%- comment -%}
  Brand lockup — the merchant's uploaded logo (Theme settings → Brand & SEO),
  or the store's own name typeset in the display face when none is set.

  The fallback used to be an inline onerror handler that swapped a broken <img>
  for a <span> in JS. That only ran AFTER the browser had already requested a
  missing asset (a guaranteed 404 on every page of a fresh install) and it put
  the lockup one failed request behind first paint. The branch belongs in Liquid,
  where it costs nothing and nothing 404s.

  Sizing rides --logo-size so every caller (header, footer, password) keeps a
  consistent visual scale for the wordmark.
{%- endcomment -%}
<span class="brand__row">
  {%- if settings.brand_logo != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%} x-descriptors, not w/sizes: the rendered size is pinned by CSS
    height, not by the viewport, so the only variable is device pixel ratio. {%- endcomment -%}
    <img class="brand__mark brand__mark--img"
      src="{{ settings.brand_logo | image_url: width: 240 }}"
      srcset="{{ settings.brand_logo | image_url: width: 240 }} 1x, {{ settings.brand_logo | image_url: width: 480 }} 2x"
      alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
      width="{{ settings.brand_logo.width }}" height="{{ settings.brand_logo.height }}"
      style="display:block; height: calc(var(--logo-size, 28px) * .82); width: auto;"
      loading="eager" decoding="async">
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="brand__mark brand__mark--text">{{ shop.name }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
